<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka 12-month T-bill yields fall.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka 12-month T-bill yields fall.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lankan treasury bill average yields were mixed at Wednesday's auction. Yields of 12-month bills fell 0.05 percentage points while those of six-month bills remained unchanged, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>Yields of three-month bills rose 0.09 percentage points.</p>
<p>		   Bids received   Bids accepted   Avg yield</p>
<p>    3 months	 951		 951	  10.91 (10.82)</p>
<p>    6 months     1,050		 445	  12.08 (12.08)</p>
<p>    12 months	834		 580	  12.87 (12.92)</p>
<p>    Total	  2,835	     1,976</p>
<p>NOTE - Bids in million rupees, yields in percent (previous week's yields in brackets).</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
